# Build output. Nothing under here is an input to anything.
/target

# Cargo.lock is deliberately absent from this file, and now it is tracked as
# well. It is not build output: it is the record of which versions a build
# actually resolved, and a reconstruction has to be reproducible from the same
# input years later. Ignoring it would leave every clone free to resolve
# something else and call the result the same program. What refuses that is
# --locked on the build, test and lint jobs in .github/workflows/ci.yml.
